nReleased on 2026-10-05.\n\nLong clips on the timeline now mount only the picture tiles in view, so a ten-minute clip scrolls and zooms smoothly, and dragging a keyframe's path node moves only that keyframe while the others stay put.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- **Studio:** Dragging a keyframe's path node keeps the other keyframes where they were ([cd0d04e4e983](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/cd0d04e4e983a71b5720a8248176a0cd2c7d3518), [#4946](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/4946)).\n\n## Performance\n\n- **Studio:** Long clips mount only the picture tiles in view ([1bdb5edd93bb](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/1bdb5edd93bb7fe58cbb5ec81133a23deb075ad2), [#4993](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/4993)).\n\n## Internal\n\n- **Core:** The HTML scanner's linear-work checks count work instead of timing it ([e703c39cdd7b](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/e703c39cdd7bfcc8ba92750610e6662d193c39f3), [#5037](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/5037)).\n\n## Full changelog\n\nhttps://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/compare/v0.8.126...v0.8.127\n"}
